  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**:  \n   - Use hierarchical resolution (45\u219260\u219290\u2192120) if improvements are found.  \n   - Repair impossible candidates with clamping and sum adjustment.  \n   - Minimize overlapping under [0,1] constraints.  \n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**:  \n   - Objective: Minimize C_5 using non-normalized cross-correlation.  \n   - Repair: Enforce [0,1] bounds and integral=1 via iterative clipping.  \n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**:  \n   - Read step size/time, target sum(n/2).  \n   - `repair(x, n)` adjusts for [0,1] and sum(n/2).  \n   - `compute_c5(h, n)` computes C_5 from cross-correlation.  \n   - CMA-ES optimization at each resolution.  \n\n4. **Search Choices**:  \n   - Starts with repair to enforce constraints before optimization.  \n   - Budget: Per resolution \u223c25% of initial, increasing n from 45 to 120.  \n\n5. **Budget and Robustness**:  \n   - Time \u221d n\u00b2. Use 50%, 25%, 10% per resolution.  \n   - Safety bounds in optimization.  \n\n6. **Validation**:  \n   - Repair ensures [0,1] and sum=1.  \n   - Return (h, c5, n) if better than parent.",
